IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-owner`
IMPORT `cat-qa`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (cat-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE (the
-- situation does not hold) and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the owner (the baseline's
-- seat) the answers are worked by hand and also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts.
-- For the person getting a cat and the veterinarian or implanter they are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts: Chloe's cat Biscuit (c076, 14 February 2036), with the baseline's assumed date of birth, 1 October 2035, so
-- Biscuit reaches 6 months on 1 April 2036. Other facts are the encoder's illustrations, as in the baseline's cases.
-- Expected values are written by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the output.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own or keep a cat`
`as the new owner` MEANS `I am getting a cat from its owner, by sale or as a gift`
`as the vet` MEANS `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter`
`Biscuit's birthday` MEANS Date 1 10 2035
`14 February 2036` MEANS Date 14 2 2036
`1 April 2036` MEANS Date 1 4 2036

§§ `For the owner: the situation holds, and the answer is the baseline's`

-- s 4.
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this cat under the Act` `as the owner` `I am the person it is registered to` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this cat under the Act` `as the owner` `I ordinarily keep and care for it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this cat under the Act` `as the owner` `I ordinarily keep and care for it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of this cat under the Act` `as the owner` `my name is on its microchip database record` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I the owner of this cat` `my name is on its microchip database record` FALSE TRUE)
-- The 6-month day: 1 April 2036 for Biscuit; 1 March 2036 for a cat born 31 August 2035.
#ASSERT `On what day does my cat reach 6 months of age` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` EQUALS `on` `1 April 2036`
#ASSERT `On what day does my cat reach 6 months of age` `as the owner` (Date 31 8 2035) EQUALS `on` (Date 1 3 2036)
#ASSERT `On what day does my cat reach 6 months of age` `as the owner` (Date 29 8 2035) EQUALS `on` (`When does my cat reach 6 months of age` (Date 29 8 2035))
-- s 5.
#ASSERT `Must my cat be registered` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `14 February 2036` 30 5000 `at home with me` 0 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 5(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be registered` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `1 April 2036` 77 5000 `at home with me` 0 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: register it with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept (s 5(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be registered` `as the owner` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` 10 5000 `at home with me` 0 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no: I have kept the cat for less than 14 days (s 5(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be registered` `as the owner` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` 100 5000 `in foster care placed by a SAFE entity` 10 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` (`Must I have my cat registered` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` 100 5000 `in foster care placed by a SAFE entity` 10 FALSE)
-- s 6, reg 10: the tag in a public place, but not at a recognised show.
#ASSERT `Must my cat wear its registration tag` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must my cat wear its registration tag` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must my cat wear its registration tag` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must my cat wear its registration tag` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must my cat be wearing its tag` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 14.
#ASSERT `Must my cat be microchipped` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `14 February 2036` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 14(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be microchipped` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `1 April 2036` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: have it microchipped by a microchip implanter (s 14(1), reg 8)`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be microchipped` `as the owner` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` (`Must I have my cat microchipped` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 18.
#ASSERT `Must my cat be sterilised` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `14 February 2036` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be sterilised` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `1 April 2036` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes, and it is sterilised (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be sterilised` `as the owner` `Biscuit's birthday` `1 April 2036` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: have it sterilised by a veterinarian (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my cat be sterilised` `as the owner` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` (`Must I have my cat sterilised` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 9: Biscuit registered early, already microchipped and sterilised: not refused; not yet sterilised: refused.
#ASSERT `Must the local government refuse my application to register my cat` `as the owner` TRUE `Biscuit's birthday` `14 February 2036` FALSE `at home with me` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `the answer is` `not to be refused, if the local government is satisfied of none of the s 9(2) grounds`
#ASSERT `Must the local government refuse my application to register my cat` `as the owner` TRUE `Biscuit's birthday` `14 February 2036` FALSE `at home with me` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `the answer is` `refused: my cat is not sterilised (s 9(2)(d))`
#ASSERT `Must the local government refuse my application to register my cat` `as the owner` TRUE (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` TRUE `at home with me` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `the answer is` `refused: I am under 18 (s 9(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must the local government refuse my application to register my cat` `as the owner` TRUE (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` FALSE `at home with me` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS `the answer is` (`Must my registration be refused` (Date 1 1 2030) `14 February 2036` FALSE `at home with me` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2)
-- Sch 3.
#ASSERT `What is the most my cat's registration fee can be` `as the owner` TRUE `one year` FALSE `14 February 2036` FALSE EQUALS amount 20
#ASSERT `What is the most my cat's registration fee can be` `as the owner` TRUE `one year` FALSE (Date 1 6 2036) FALSE EQUALS amount 10
#ASSERT `What is the most my cat's registration fee can be` `as the owner` TRUE `3 years` FALSE `14 February 2036` TRUE EQUALS amount 21.25
#ASSERT `What is the most my cat's registration fee can be` `as the owner` TRUE `the life of the cat` FALSE `14 February 2036` FALSE EQUALS amount (`What is the most my registration fee can be` `the life of the cat` FALSE `14 February 2036` FALSE)
-- reg 12.
#ASSERT `When will my cat's registration end` `as the owner` TRUE `one year` `14 February 2036` EQUALS `the answer is` (`on 31 October` (Date 31 10 2036))
#ASSERT `When will my cat's registration end` `as the owner` TRUE `3 years` `14 February 2036` EQUALS `the answer is` (`on 31 October` (Date 31 10 2038))
#ASSERT `When will my cat's registration end` `as the owner` TRUE `the life of the cat` `14 February 2036` EQUALS `the answer is` `on the death of the cat, unless cancelled sooner`
#ASSERT `When will my cat's registration end` `as the owner` TRUE `one year` (Date 31 10 2036) EQUALS `the answer is` (`When does my cat's registration end` `one year` (Date 31 10 2036))
#ASSERT `Can I renew my cat's registration today to take effect from 1 November` `as the owner` TRUE (Date 11 10 2036) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I renew my cat's registration today to take effect from 1 November` `as the owner` TRUE (Date 10 10 2036) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I renew my cat's registration today to take effect from 1 November` `as the owner` TRUE (Date 31 10 2036) EQUALS `yes if` (`Can I renew today to take effect from 1 November` (Date 31 10 2036))
-- s 23, reg 19.
#ASSERT `May I give away or sell my cat as it is` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `not unless it is microchipped first (s 23(1))`
#ASSERT `May I give away or sell my cat as it is` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes (s 23)`
#ASSERT `May I give away or sell my cat as it is` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `not unless it is sterilised first, or I give the new owner a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `May I give away or sell my cat as it is` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` (`May I give away or sell my cat` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 25: 7 days.
#ASSERT `By what day must I give notice of the change to my details` `as the owner` TRUE `14 February 2036` EQUALS `by` (Date 21 2 2036)
#ASSERT `By what day must I give notice of the change to my details` `as the owner` TRUE (Date 28 2 2036) EQUALS `by` (`By when must I give notice of the change` (Date 28 2 2036))
-- s 79(3)(h), ULP regs 5-7.
#ASSERT `How many cats may I keep at my home` `as the owner` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the answer is` `no number is set by the Act or the uniform regulations; a local law may set one (s 79(3)(h))`
#ASSERT `How many cats may I keep at my home` `as the owner` TRUE 2 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the answer is` (`at most this many cats aged 6 months or more` 2)
#ASSERT `How many cats may I keep at my home` `as the owner` TRUE 2 TRUE 1 EQUALS `the answer is` (`How many cats may I keep here` TRUE 2 TRUE 1)
-- The fines.
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this cat offence` `as the owner` `cat not registered (s 5(1))` EQUALS amount 5000
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this cat offence` `as the owner` `cat not sterilised (s 18(1))` EQUALS amount (`What is the most I can be fined` `cat not sterilised (s 18(1))`)
#ASSERT `How much is an infringement notice for this cat offence` `as the owner` `keeping more than the standard number of cats (ULP reg 6(1))` EQUALS amount 200
#ASSERT `How much is an infringement notice for this cat offence` `as the owner` `cat not registered (s 5(1))` EQUALS amount (`How much is the infringement notice` `cat not registered (s 5(1))`)

§§ `For the person getting a cat (worked by hand)`

#ASSERT `May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` `as the new owner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not unless it is microchipped first: the owner commits an offence otherwise (s 23(1))`
#ASSERT `May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` `as the new owner` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not unless it is sterilised first, or the owner gives you a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` `as the new owner` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes (s 23)`
#ASSERT `May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` `as the new owner` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes (s 23)`
#ASSERT `May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` `as the new owner` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes (s 23)`
#ASSERT `May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` `as the new owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are a body named in reg 9, so s 23 does not apply (reg 19)`

§§ `For the veterinarian or microchip implanter (worked by hand)`

-- ss 14(3), 18(3): no certificate for Biscuit on 14 February 2036; from 1 April 2036 it can apply.
#ASSERT `Can my certificate exempting this cat from microchipping or sterilisation apply to it` `as the vet` `Biscuit's birthday` `14 February 2036` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my certificate exempting this cat from microchipping or sterilisation apply to it` `as the vet` `Biscuit's birthday` (Date 31 3 2036) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my certificate exempting this cat from microchipping or sterilisation apply to it` `as the vet` `Biscuit's birthday` `1 April 2036` EQUALS yes
-- s 15: implanted on 14 February 2036; notice by 21 February.
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the database company about the microchip I implanted` `as the vet` TRUE `14 February 2036` EQUALS `by` (Date 21 2 2036)
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the database company about the microchip I implanted` `as the vet` TRUE (Date 28 12 2036) EQUALS `by` (Date 4 1 2037)
-- s 20: only for a microchipped cat; the day is not read for one that is not.
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the database company that I sterilised the cat` `as the vet` TRUE TRUE (Date 25 2 2036) EQUALS `by` (Date 3 3 2036)
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the database company that I sterilised the cat` `as the vet` TRUE FALSE `an unasked date` EQUALS `no notice is needed: the cat is not microchipped (s 20)`
-- s 21, s 17, the fines.
#ASSERT `Must I give the owner a certificate of sterilisation` `as the vet` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I remove or interfere with a microchip in a cat` `as the vet` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I remove or interfere with a microchip in a cat` `as the vet` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for breaking a veterinarian's or implanter's duty` `as the vet` EQUALS amount 5000

§§ `Every question, for the roles it is not about, and with its situation not holding: nothing else is read`

